  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1202 PM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nToday, we will see our coldest temperatures of the season so far \nwith lows dipping down to the low 40s through much of the lowlands. \nArea mountains will see subfreezing conditions with the Sacs \nreaching the low 20s in some parts during tomorrow's early morning. \nThese temperature trends are about 15 to 20 degrees below normal for \nthis time of year. High temperatures will rebound by the end of the \nweekend. Widespread sustained easterly winds between 20 and 30 mph \nwill continue this afternoon and evening with gusts exceeding 50 mph \nat times in parts of southern Hidalgo county.\n\nBlowing dust remains a concern through this evening coinciding with \nthe greatest wind threat in southern Hidalgo county according to the \nsignatures in the RRFS. A Blowing Dust Advisory near the Lordsburg \nPlaya, NM Bootheel, and Luna county is in effect through 8 PM \ntonight.\n\nWinds subside and precip chances are rather slim for most of the \nweekend with greater chances favoring the western half of the CWA on \nSunday morning as a developing upper level low pushes east. This low \ndeepens considerably over the course of next week bringing with it \nincreasing chances for precip. Flooding is possible with areawide \nrain and PWs reaching around 1 inch. Confidence remains low for \nmidweek rain impacts at this time.",
